# CODEOWNERS — The Council
#
# Routing rules for review attention. The repo is single-maintainer
# today; this file is the seam for adding domain co-owners later
# (security, compliance, accessibility, infra) without a structural
# rewrite. Each section names the file globs + the owners who must
# approve the PR.
#
# Order matters: the LAST matching rule wins. Place narrower globs
# below broader ones.
#
# Reference: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-
# repositories-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/
# about-code-owners

# ── Default — everything routes to the maintainer ───────────────
*                                                           @nmor

# ── Council protocol + Core rules ───────────────────────────────
# Changes here ripple through every consumer; review at the rules
# Division level (Architecture + Compliance + Security).
/CLAUDE.md                                                  @nmor
/rules/common/council-default.md                            @nmor
/rules/common/council-triggers.md                           @nmor
/rules/common/principal-level-mandate.md                    @nmor
/rules/common/task-intake-due-diligence.md                  @nmor
/rules/common/verify-before-claim.md                        @nmor
/rules/common/no-overclaim.md                               @nmor

# ── Security-sensitive rules ────────────────────────────────────
# Security division territory. Bumping these forwards lands in
# every consumer repo's auto-load set.
/rules/common/security.md                                   @nmor
/rules/common/secrets-management.md                         @nmor
/rules/common/security-controls-org-wide.md                 @nmor
/rules/common/install-allowlist.md                          @nmor
/rules/common/dependency-vulnerabilities.md                 @nmor
/rules/common/dependency-overrides-not-exceptions.md        @nmor
/rules/common/license-allowlist-gate.md                     @nmor
/rules/common/docker-localhost-binding.md                   @nmor
/rules/common/no-local-fs.md                                @nmor

# ── Compliance + privacy ────────────────────────────────────────
/rules/common/gdpr-ccpa.md                                  @nmor
/rules/common/data-retention.md                             @nmor
/rules/common/audit-logging.md                              @nmor
/rules/common/code-of-conduct.md                            @nmor

# ── Verifiers + CI gates ────────────────────────────────────────
# These are the source of truth for "is the repo healthy?". Any
# change to verifier logic needs an extra-careful read.
/bootstrap/                                                 @nmor
/tests/                                                     @nmor
/.github/workflows/                                         @nmor

# ── Install + cross-platform surface ────────────────────────────
# Consumers run these as their FIRST command. Bugs here block
# adoption. Review with cross-platform discipline (bash 3.2 on
# macOS + bash 5.x on Ubuntu + PowerShell on Windows).
/bootstrap/install.sh                                       @nmor
/bootstrap/install.ps1                                      @nmor
/bootstrap/verify.sh                                        @nmor
/ide-integrations/                                          @nmor

# ── Repo governance + supply-chain ──────────────────────────────
# Tag-protection + branch-protection settings outside this file
# also gate these (configured at repo-settings level). Listed
# here so any change to the governance surface gets review.
/.github/CODEOWNERS                                         @nmor
/.github/dependabot.yml                                     @nmor
/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md                           @nmor
/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/                                    @nmor
/SECURITY.md                                                @nmor
/LICENSE                                                    @nmor
/CHANGELOG.md                                               @nmor
